  "title": "Invention of gunpowder",
  "summary": "In the mid-ninth century, according to EBSCO, Daoist alchemists in China found that sulfur, saltpeter and a carbon material such as charcoal made a flammable mixture. A Harvard thesis says a ninth-century Daoist text warned against combining them. EBSCO says the first book with a gunpowder formula appeared in 1044.",
